      "message": "I should ask, would it not be better to do an upstream list discussion on this before even a common-kernel or pixel kernel merge? I know it was presented at LPC and that\u0027s great, but there should be some RFC posted involving:\n  - Rafael Wysocki (cpufreq, schedutil)\n  - Patrick Belasi (uclamp)\n  - Viresh (for his opinion on these things)\n  - Paulo Bonzini (KVM) and Marc Zyngier (arm64 KVM)\n  \n(I am sorry if I missed something, if so - please provide links).\n  \nMy fear is whole thing makes its way into downstream kernels through AOSP, and then it becomes forever-debt after few years, like WALT or any number of examples. I don\u0027t mind downstream / common kernel push, but that should be after exhaustive upstream discussion. Very least a discussion prevents a bad design because one did not consider something (apologies for cliche).\n\nAlso, I am still of the opinion of finding some way to use the vcpu\u0027s guest util on the host side, and let the host do the right thing.\n\nJust my suggestion/opinion! I will refrain from providing an AOSP gerrit vote (positive or negative). Thanks.",
